xists so only `.value` is overwritten) | [x] |\n\n## Notes on assert rows\n\nRows 23, 35, 36, 37, 38, 44 and 50 are `assert`s that are **not reachable\nthrough the public API** while the caller respects the library's own\ninvariants. The Rust translation omits them (they are comments in\n`translation/src/lib.rs`). Because the C asserts can never fire on any input a\nlegitimate caller can produce, omitting them is behaviour-preserving. Each such\nrow is discharged by an argument above plus, where cheap, a differential test\nthat drives the surrounding branch to completion without tripping the assert.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
