{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_g27irzje4rb2q5j6qwacg5ufs7gahlja472qj74wagjwyal2xmbq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Audit complete. I read both files fully, compared every listed function line-by-line, and validated the analysis with a dynamic differential harness (dlopen both `.so`s side by side) targeting exactly the bug classes you listed.\n\n## Confirmed divergences\n\n### D1. `stbds_stralloc` — shift-amount panic (your class 7). REAL, reproduced.\n- C lib.c:888: `blocksize = (size_t) (STBDS_STRING_ARENA_BLOCKSIZE_MIN) << (blocksize>>1);` where `blocksize = a->block` (`unsigned char`, 0..255).\n- Rust src/lib.rs:1074: `blocksize = STBDS_STRING_ARENA_BLOCKSIZE_MIN << (blocksize >> 1);`\n- Concrete input: call `stbds_stralloc(&arena, \"hello\")` with a caller-owned zeroed `stbds_string_arena` whose `block` field is set to **128** (or anything ≥ 128, so `block>>1 >= 64`).\n  - C (gcc, `shl` masks count to `&63`): shift count becomes `64&63 == 0`, `blocksize = 512`, function returns normally → measured `remaining = 506`.\n  - Rust debug: `attempt to shift left with overflow` → panic at `src/lib.rs:1074:21` → non-unwinding panic → **abort**.\n  - Measured: `block=128` → C `ok p=hello block_after=129 remaining=506`; Rust `panicked at src/lib.rs:1074`. `block=250` → C `ok ... remaining=0`; Rust aborts. Boundary is exactly 128 (`block=126`/`127` agree: both give `remaining=0`).\n- Rust *release* (`opt-level=3`) masks the shift the same way gcc does, so this is a debug-build-only behavioral break, but it is a hard abort vs. a normal return.\n- Not reachable through the library's own logic (`a->block` self-caps at 22, since `++a->block` stops once `512<<(block>>1) >= 1<<20`), but `stbds_stralloc` is an exported entry point taking a caller-supplied arena, so a differential harness can reach it.\n\n### D2. All seven `STBDS_ASSERT` calls are missing from the Rust (your class 8). REAL, reproduced for one of them.\nThe C `.so` is built with **no** `-DNDEBUG` (`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` is empty in `c_src/build/CMakeCache.txt`; `nm -D --undefined-only` shows `U __assert_fail@GLIBC_2.2.5`), so asserts are live. Rust has them as comments (lib.rs:336, 1110) or dropped entirely.\n\nDropped: lib.c:401, 778, 828, 832, 846, 849, 913.\n\nOnly lib.c:846 is reachable, and it is:\n- C lib.c:846: `STBDS_ASSERT(slot >= 0);`\n- Rust src/lib.rs:1029 goes straight to `b = (*table).storage.offset(slot >> STBDS_BUCKET_SHIFT);` with no check.\n- Concrete input: `mode = 2` (the `STBDS_HM_PTR_TO_STRING` value that `stbds_pshput`/`stbds_pshdel` at lib.c:188/209 pass, though the constant isn't defined in this TU). Insert `\"alpha\",\"beta\",\"gamma\",\"delta\"` via `stbds_hmput_key(..., keysize=8, mode=2)`, then `stbds_hmdel_key(t, 16, \"alpha\", 8, offsetof(key), 2)`. Because lib.c:842 uses `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` (false for 2), line 845 re-finds the moved slot with the *binary* key expression while `stbds_hm_find_slot` still hashes it as a string (`mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING`), so `slot == -1`.\n  - C: `a: .../lib.c:846: stbds_hmdel_key: Assertion 'slot >= 0' failed.` → SIGABRT, exit 134.\n  - Rust: returns normally (exit 0) after `storage.offset(-1)` and an out-of-bounds `(*b).index[i] = old_index` write.\n- The other six asserts are provably non-firing for any input (401: threshold ratio is 0.75+0.1875 < 1 for all reachable `slot_count >= 8`; 778: `arrgrowf` guarantees `cap >= min_len`; 828: `find_slot` returns `< slot_count`; 832: `size_t >= 0`; 849/913: hold under the internal invariants).\n\n## Everything else in your list: equivalent\n\nVerified statically and, where observable, dynamically (0 mismatches over: 16 400 `stbds_hash_bytes` cases, len 0..40, bytes biased to `0x00/0x80/0xff`; 20 000 `stbds_hash_string` cases with high-bit chars; 5 000 `stbds_stralloc`+`stbds_strreset` ops comparing `remaining`/`block`; 6 000-step randomized op mixes of `hmput_key`/`hmget_key`/`hmget_key_ts`/`hmdel_key`/`hmput_default`/`shmode_func`/`hmfree_func` in `SH_DEFAULT`/`SH_STRDUP`/`SH_ARENA` string modes and in binary mode, comparing `length`, `temp`, `slot_count`, `used_count`, `tombstone_count`, `string.mode`, `string.block`, whole array contents, and `temp_key`-was-set; and byte-exact `helxo`/`strkey` stdout for 38 `letter` values including `letter=0`).\n\n1. **Signedness/promotion in `stbds_siphash_bytes`.** lib.c:523 `data = d[0]|(d[1]<<8)|(d[2]<<16)|(d[3]<<24)` is `int` and sign-extends — Rust:489-493 reproduces it exactly via `i32 → i64 → usize`. lib.c:524 `(size_t)(...)<<16<<16`: the sign extension is *discarded* by the `<<32`, and Rust:495-499 matches. lib.c:536 `case 4: data |= (d[3] << 24);` sign-extends — Rust:525 `((((*d.add(3) as u32) << 24) as i32) as i64) as usize` matches. lib.c:537/538/539 are non-negative `int`s; Rust:528/531/534 match. lib.c:533/534/535 (`<<24<<24`, `<<20<<20`, `<<16<<16` = shifts of 48/40/32) match Rust:515/518/521.\n2. **`stbds_load_32_or_64`** (lib.c:360-363 at 410-411): `0x87b0b0fd` and `0xb504f32d` are `unsigned int` (hex constants > INT_MAX), so `v64_lo ^ v32` is computed in `unsigned int` and zero-extends; `2147001325`, `715136305`, `0x27bb2ee6` are non-negative `int`. Rust:278-291 takes all three as `u32` and zero-extends — identical. Produces `a = 0x27bb2ee687b0b0fd`, `b = 0x00000000b504f32d` in both; the `<<16<<16>>16>>16` sequence is a no-op on a zero-extended 32-bit value in both.\n3. **Assignment chains.** lib.c:708 `stbds_header(a)->hash_table = table = nt;` → Rust:795-796 assigns `nt` to both. lib.c:786-788 `stbds_temp_key(a) = *(char**)(...) = f(...)` (right-assoc: slot written first, then `temp_key` gets the same value) → Rust:908-925 `*slot = f(...); stbds_temp_key_set(a, *slot);`. The two destinations never alias (array storage vs. separately `realloc`'d hash index). Equivalent.\n4. **Fall-through.** lib.c:532 `switch (len - i)` cases 7→0 all fall through; `len - i` is provably 0..7, and Rust:514-535's descending `if rem >= 7 … if rem >= 1` chain is exactly that. lib.c:785 `switch (table->string.mode)` has a `break` in every arm and Rust:910-934 uses non-fall-through `match` guards. Both correct.\n5. **`>=` vs `==` on `mode`.** `>=`: lib.c:560→lib.rs:568, lib.c:590→lib.rs:614, lib.c:713→lib.rs:800, plus lib.c:707→lib.rs:789 and lib.c:732→lib.rs:833. `==`: lib.c:836→lib.rs:987, lib.c:842→lib.rs:1004. All preserved (this asymmetry is what makes D2 reachable).\n6. **Truncating casts.** lib.c:803 `(unsigned char) mode` → lib.rs:948 `mode as u8`. lib.c:825 `int i = slot & STBDS_BUCKET_MASK;` → lib.rs:978 `((slot as usize) & STBDS_BUCKET_MASK) as c_int` (same result even for negative `slot`: `-1 & 7 == 7` both ways).\n7. **Wrapping arithmetic.** `2 * stbds_arrcap(a)` (lib.c:289-290 → `wrapping_mul`, lib.rs:232-233), `elemsize * min_cap + sizeof(header)` (lib.c:297 → lib.rs:243), `stbds_hash_seed * a + b` (lib.c:412 → lib.rs:355), `len << (STBDS_SIZE_T_BITS-8)` (lib.c:531 → lib.rs:511), `hash += 2` (lib.c:596/719 → lib.rs:624/811, guarded by `hash < 2`), `pos += step` (→ `wrapping_add`), `table->slot_count*2` (lib.c:702 → lib.rs:783). Non-wrapping Rust operators remain at lib.rs:298 (`slot_count - 1`), 890 (`tombstone_count -= 1`), 981 (`used_count -= 1`), 1033 (`length -= 1`), 1114 (`remaining -= len`) — each is unreachable at the wrap boundary given the invariants (`slot_count >= 8` always; `tombstone_count` equals the number of `INDEX_DELETED` entries because every rebuild/grow/shrink drops them and resets it to 0; `used_count > 0` whenever `find_slot` succeeded).\n8. **Rotates.** `STBDS_ROTATE_LEFT/RIGHT` are only instantiated with 9, 11, 13, 16, 17, 21, 22, 31, 32 — never 0 and never ≥ 64 — so neither the C UB nor a Rust shift panic is reachable.\n9. **`helxo` variadic struct pass (lib.c:959).** ABI-equivalent. `{char* key; char value;}` is 16 bytes / classes (INTEGER, INTEGER), so it occupies `rsi` (= `key`) and `rdx` (low byte = `value`, bytes 1..7 indeterminate padding); the third arg (`hash[z].value`, in `rcx`) is never consumed by `\"%s %c\\n\"`. glibc's `%c` reads `(unsigned char) va_arg(int)`, i.e. only the low byte of `rdx`, so Rust's `printf(c\"%s %c\\n\", key, value as c_int)` (lib.rs:1219-1223) yields byte-identical output — verified with `diff` over all 38 tested `letter` values, including `letter == 0` (both emit a raw NUL). Rust hoisting `shlen(hash)` out of the loop (lib.rs:1216) is equivalent because nothing in the body changes the length or reassigns `hash`.\n\nAlso equivalent (spot-checked): `STBDS_ALIGN_FWD` mask width (C's `~(64-1)` is `int -64`, converted to `size_t` = `0xFFFF…FFC0`, same as Rust's `!(63usize)`); the `goto done` / `goto found_empty_slot` control flow rendered as labeled `break`s (lib.rs:383-411, 816-885) — `break 'outer` out of the inner `loop` lands at the same place as C's `done:` label inside the `for j` body; the second inner probe loop's deliberate omission of `stbds_temp_key` (lib.c:749-750 vs. 731-733) is preserved at lib.rs:868 vs. 832-840; `stbds_hmput_key`'s memset-before-length++ (lib.c:688-689) vs. `stbds_hmget_key_ts`'s length++-before-memset (lib.c:636-637) are both preserved.\n\nOne housekeeping note: I could not delete my scratch harness — `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-6M6KAs/.audit-tmp/` (C sources + binaries, ~7 files) is left behind because `rm` was denied by the permission system. It is outside both `c_src/` and `translation/`. No files under audit were modified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1750,"cache_read_input_tokens":116347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1750,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01HeXZnFaUy7BgPVe1h3oPcv","session_id":"e2dcfccc-b98f-4c68-871b-22e93296d372","uuid":"57b7977d-e81d-445e-9c09-6ee0050ce6dc","timestamp":"2026-09-05T08:44:5