{"duration_api_ms":2678180,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e2dcfccc-b98f-4c68-871b-22e93296d372","total_cost_usd":21.23131100000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":80,"cache_creation_input_tokens":297883,"cache_read_input_tokens":10717768,"output_tokens":31690,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8058},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":297883},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"global.anthropic.claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":270,"outputTokens":217480,"cacheReadInputTokens":23363422,"cacheCreationInputTokens":657800,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":21.23131100000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":68281,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"bedrock","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JdYevoN52GtPZ6V4Buypcf","tool_input":{"command":"rm -rf /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-6M6KAs/.audit-tmp /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-6M6KAs/.repro 2>&1; ls -a /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-6M6KAs | grep -E \"audit|repro\" || echo \"scratch dirs removed\"","description":"Remove audit and repro scratch dirs"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"not_first_party","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"subagent_stats":{"spawned":1,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":1},"started_in_background":1,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":1,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"general-purpose":1}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":40,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Verification complete. **The audit found two real divergences that the in-process suite had missed; both are now fixed and covered by regression tests.**\n\n## Divergences found & fixed (`translation/src/lib.rs`)\n\n**1. `stbds_stralloc` shift-count overflow** (`lib.c:888`)\n`blocksize = 512 << (a->block >> 1)` — `a->block` is an `unsigned char` the **caller** owns, so the count reaches 127. Rust used a bare `<<` → *panic + abort* in debug builds where the C returns normally.\nI reproduced it against the real `.so`s: `block=128` → C `remaining=506` / Rust debug `thread caused non-unwinding panic`. Every `block ≥ 128` broke.\nFix: mask the count with `& (STBDS_SIZE_T_BITS - 1)`, matching the `shlq %cl` the C compiles to (confirmed empirically: `block=128` → `blocksize=512`, `block=254` → `blocksize=0`).\n\n**2. All seven `STBDS_ASSERT`s were missing** — and one is *reachable*\nThe C `.so` is built with no `-DNDEBUG` (`nm -D` shows `U __assert_fail`), so asserts are live. `assert(slot >= 0)` at `lib.c:846` fires when `mode == 2`: `lib.c:842` tests `mode == STBDS_HM_STRING` (false) while `hm_find_slot` tests `mode >= STBDS_HM_STRING` (true), so the re-find hashes raw element bytes as a string, misses, and returns `-1`.\nReproduced: C → `SIGABRT` + `lib.c:846: stbds_hmdel_key: Assertion \\`slot >= 0' failed.`; Rust → returned `survived, len=4` after `storage.offset(-1)` and an **out-of-bounds write**.\nFix: all seven asserts translated through glibc's `__assert_fail` with matching text/function/line — same message body, same SIGABRT.\n\nNote: matching this needed an **out-of-process** harness (`tests/aborts.rs`, compiles a small `dlopen` helper and compares child exit status/signal/stderr) — no in-process differential test can observe it.\n\n## Final state\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Symbol parity | 0 missing, 0 extra (16 symbols) |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 78 rows, all ✅ |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 64 rows, all ✅ |\n| Matrix | **58 tests × {debug, release} × {plain, `MALLOC_CHECK_=3 MALLOC_PERTURB_=42`} → ALL CONFIGURATIONS PASSED**, 0 warnings |\n\nOne documented **non**-divergence: the C never checks any allocation result, so on real OOM it dereferences NULL. Rust release reproduces that exactly (both SIGSEGV); Rust debug's null-deref assertion turns it into SIGABRT. Only observable outside the C's defined behaviour, so `tests/aborts.rs` classifies each case dynamically from the C's own exit status rather than assuming an outcome.\n\nTwo things to flag:\n- The earlier \"no divergence found\" conclusion in my previous message was **wrong** — the in-process suite was green but blind to process-terminating behaviour. The independent audit is what caught it.\n- Scratch dirs `.audit-tmp/` and `.repro/` remain at the workspace root; `rm` was denied by the sandbox, so please delete them manually. Neither `c_src/` nor anything else was modified.","ttft_ms":20764,"type":"result","duration_ms":948133,"uuid":"bef1c2b6-f8e7-4c90-8cf2-3d18d1fdbd45","ttft_stream_ms":2291,"time_to_request_ms":16,"first_content_frame_ms":2742,"queued_turn_count":0}
